cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this pipeline or the datasets it produces in your research,
  please cite the repository as below.
title: "IWAC Hugging Face Pipeline"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-05
abstract: >-
  Python pipeline that mirrors the Islam West Africa Collection (IWAC) from an
  Omeka S archive into versioned Hugging Face datasets. It maps seven subsets
  (articles, audiovisual, documents, images, index, publications, references)
  from the Omeka S REST API, enriches them with computed columns — semantic
  embeddings, spaCy lemmas, LDA topics, lexical metrics, Islamic-calendar dates
  and a multi-model sentiment panel — and projects the result into a public
  dataset in which full text is masked per row according to the access status
  of the source item. Built for the Islam West Africa Collection and adaptable
  to other Omeka S collections published as research datasets.
type: software
keywords:
  - digital humanities
  - Islam West Africa
  - Omeka S
  - Hugging Face
  - research data management
  - topic modeling
  - semantic embeddings
  - sentiment analysis
  - corpus linguistics
  - African studies
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/fmadore/IWAC-Hugging-Face
# Landing page for the project as a whole. The dataset has its own URL and DOI
# under `references` below; this field describes the software.
url: https://islam.zmo.de/s/westafrica/
authors:
  - family-names: Madore
    given-names: Frédérick
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0959-2092
    affiliation: University of Bayreuth
# DOIs — two different objects, two different registries:
#
#   * This repository is the CODE. Archive it on Zenodo via the GitHub
#     integration (it only sees public repos) and add the CONCEPT DOI below —
#     the one that always resolves to the newest version, which is what a
#     citation should point at. Mirrors iwac-ai-pipelines (10.5281/zenodo.21804210).
#
#   * The DATASET is cited separately with a Hugging Face DOI, minted from the
#     dataset's Settings page and issued through DataCite. Mint it on the
#     PUBLIC repo only. Do NOT mint one on islam-west-africa-collection-full:
#     a DOI locks deletion, renaming and visibility changes behind a support
#     request, and it would not resolve for anyone without access anyway.
#     Note that HF assigns a new DOI per revision and marks the previous one
#     outdated; it has no version-independent concept DOI.
#
# identifiers:
#   - type: doi
#     value: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXXX   # Zenodo concept DOI (this pipeline)
#
# The dataset this pipeline produces is a distinct work with its own DOI, so it
# belongs under `references` rather than `identifiers` — the latter would claim
# the dataset's DOI identifies this source code, which it does not.
references:
  - type: data
    title: "Islam West Africa Collection (IWAC)"
    doi: 10.57967/hf/9857
    url: https://huggingface.co/datasets/fmadore/islam-west-africa-collection
    year: 2025
    publisher:
      name: Leibniz-Zentrum Moderner Orient (ZMO)
    license: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
    authors:
      - family-names: Madore
        given-names: Frédérick
        orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0959-2092
        affiliation: University of Bayreuth
